<title>NETHERLANDS: Aegon, Providian - key ratios.</title>
<headline>Aegon, Providian - key ratios.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch insurer Aegon said on Monday it agreed to buy the insurance activities of Providian Corp of the United States in a deal worth $3.5 billion.</p>
<p>Following is a brief comparison of certain key ratios:</p>
<p>(All figures, from Reuters Securities 3000, relate to year-ending December 1995)</p>
<p>					     Aegon	Providian</p>
<p>    Book Value per Share	   Dfl  30.52   $ 31.60</p>
<p>    Return on Equity (pct)		16.49     13.58</p>
<p>    Return on Total Assets (pct)	 0.92	1.37</p>
<p>    Earnings per Share	     Dfl   5.04   $  3.60</p>
<p>    Investment Income (billion)  Dfl   5.98   $  1.86</p>
<p>    Market Cap (billion)	   Dfl  26.30   $  4.94</p>
<p>    Staff				    19,554     8,600</p>
<p>    Total Assets (billion)	 Dfl 150.6    $ 26.84</p>
<p>    Total Liabilities (billion)  Dfl 142.4    $ 23.88</p>
<p>    Shareholder Equity (billion) Dfl   8.09   $  2.96</p>
<p>    Claims Ratio (pct)		   107.35    147.03</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
